<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African July producer price index up 6.6 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African July producer price index up 6.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-commodities producer price index rose 0.8 percent in July from June after rising 0.7 percent in June, Central Statistical Service figures show.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in July was 6.6 percent after June's 6.1 percent rise.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast PPI would rise 0.8 percent month-on-month with a range of 0.6 to 1.0 percent. The year-on-year forecast was 6.6 percent with a range of 6.4 to 6.8 percent.  </p>
<p>    Pct changes:	     Year/year		    month/month</p>
<p>			 Jul '96   Jun '96   Jul '95  - latest   prev</p>
<p>All commodities    6.6	 6.1	 9.0	  0.8	0.7</p>
<p>Locally produced   7.3	 6.5	 9.5	  1.1	0.5</p>
<p>Imported	     4.9	 4.7	 6.4	  0.0	0.8</p>
<p>Index (base 1995=100):</p>
<p>			 Jul '96   Jun '96   Jul '95</p>
<p>All commodities    106.9     106.1     100.3</p>
<p>Locally produced   107.7     106.5     100.4</p>
<p>Imported	     104.7     104.7	99.8</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
